from __future__ import annotations

__doc__ = """
Generic builder infrastructure for lowering instruction trees to code-container
graphs.

The builder layer is the central translation stage between the backend-neutral
instruction IR and backend-specific routine containers. A :class:`Builder`
matches instruction classes to handler methods, manages namespace assignments
for ADAA-backed routine variables, expands grouped instructions into external
lookup tables and multiframe loops, and finally emits the code-container tree
consumed by language-specific libraries.

This module defines the generic :class:`Builder`, which performs the actual
lowering from instructions to code containers.

Build-chain orchestration objects such as :class:`BuilderSegment`,
:class:`Optimizer`, :class:`Validator`, and :class:`BuildChain` now live in
the separate :mod:`phoenix.fgen.buildchain` module.

Language backends such as Fortran, C, CUDA, Python, and NumPy inherit from
:class:`Builder` and override only the parts that are backend-specific:
variable creation, comments, routine-call containers, external constant arrays,
and instruction handlers.
"""

